odotengine/godot/issues/comments/2691706368","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/103416#issuecomment-2691706368","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103416","id":2691706368,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6gcC4A","user":{"login":"CreatedBySeb","id":11736217,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExNzM2MjE3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11736217?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/CreatedBySeb","html_url":"https://github.com/CreatedBySeb","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CreatedBySeb/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CreatedBySeb/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CreatedBySeb/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CreatedBySeb/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CreatedBySeb/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CreatedBySeb/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CreatedBySeb/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CreatedBySeb/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CreatedBySeb/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-02-28T23:20:15Z","updated_at":"2025-02-28T23:20:15Z","body":"Thanks for the catch, I've added a check in the `_add_animation_player` method to avoid a crash, and am working on the disable logic. I got it working for tabbing between empty and non-empty scenes, but not when the node is created in the empty scene, so I think I need to find the right signals to cover this properly. Will keep looking into it.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2691706368/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2692125330","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/103416#issuecomment-2692125330","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103416","id":2692125330,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6gdpKS","user":{"login":"CreatedBySeb","id":11736217,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExNzM2MjE3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11736217?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/CreatedBySeb","html_url":"https://github.com/CreatedBySeb","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CreatedBySeb/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CreatedBySeb/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CreatedBySeb/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CreatedBySeb/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CreatedBySeb/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CreatedBySeb/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CreatedBySeb/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CreatedBySeb/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CreatedBySeb/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-01T10:20:59Z","updated_at":"2025-03-01T10:20:59Z","body":"I have a solution now which I think works for enabling and disabling the button when the scene is empty. I have three signal connections, for when the scene is changed and for when a child is added/removed from the scene root, which disable or enable the button as appropriate. I did some testing and it seems to work alright.\r\n\r\nThe existing logic is split a bit between `animation_player_editor_plugin.cpp` and `animation_track_editor.cpp`, I've mostly modified `animation_track_editor.cpp` but I'm not sure if some of the logic should be relocated. For the follow up change on automatically selecting the AnimationPlayer node, it seems like that will probably need to live in `animation_player_editor_plugin.cpp`. Happy to get input on the proper places to locate these things.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2692125330/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2695637267","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/103416#issuecomment-2695637267","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103416","id":2695637267,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6grCkT","user":{"login":"CreatedBySeb","id":11736217,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExNzM2MjE3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11736217?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/CreatedBySeb","html_url":"https://github.com/CreatedBySeb","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CreatedBySeb/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CreatedBySeb/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CreatedBySeb/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CreatedBySeb/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CreatedBySeb/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CreatedBySeb/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CreatedBySeb/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CreatedBySeb/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CreatedBySeb/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-03T21:47:52Z","updated_at":"2025-03-03T21:48:26Z","body":"I've rebased onto the current master with the release of 4.4.\r\n\r\nI've also added a second commit which automatically selects an AnimationPlayer when it is the only one in the scene when the Animation pane opens (or is already open when switching to a scene). This change did involve swapping the order of the `edit` and `make_visible` calls in `EditorNode::_plugin_over_edit` from `editor_node.cpp`, which I was unsure about. This order would make sense to me, since I would think you would want to specify the object to be edited before making a pane visible, but I am unsure if this may affect existing code depending on it - so ideas on how to test or alternative approaches to this would be welcome. This seemed like the most straightforward way to implement this, but changing ordering like this can be risky in a big project.\r\n\r\nI have found one issue with the bottom panes, for the GridMap plugin as a result of calls down to `RendererSceneCull::instance_geometry_set_transparency`, though it's not immediately clear why when trying to debug it. If it is this one issue, fixing it may be easier than finding an alternative implementation for the player selection.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2695637267/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2695652070","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/103416#issuecomment-2695652070","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103416","id":2695652070,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6grGLm","user":{"login":"passivestar","id":60579014,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYwNTc5MDE0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/60579014?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar","html_url":"https://github.com/passivestar","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"ht